{"id":"46824c112227e4e8c1e297438d815293377b27ae","axis":"silent","repo":"expo/expo","sha":"46824c112227e4e8c1e297438d815293377b27ae","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changeset/crypto-ios-aes-error-codes.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+---","+'expo-crypto': patch","+---","+","+[iOS] AES encryption, decryption, and sealed data errors now have the `ERR_ENCRYPTION_FAILED`, `ERR_DECRYPTION_FAILED`, and `ERR_INVALID_SEALED_DATA_CONFIG` codes instead of `ERR_UNEXPECTED`. An invalid enum argument, such as an unsupported key size, now rejects with `ERR_ENUM_NO_SUCH_VALUE` instead of `ERR_ARGUMENT_CAST`."],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":".changeset/crypto-ios-aes-modules-api-2.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+---","+'expo-crypto': patch","+---","+","+[iOS] Migrate the AES encryption module to the Expo Modules API 2.0 macros, which makes calling it from JavaScript faster."],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":".changeset/crypto-ios-scan-modules.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+---","+'expo-crypto': patch","+---","+","+[iOS] Remove the module class declarations from `expo-module.config.json`. Autolinking now detects the `@ExpoModule`-annotated classes."],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"apps/bare-expo/ios/Podfile.lock","lines":["@@ -372,6 +372,12 @@ PODS:","     - ExpoModulesTestCore","   - ExpoCrypto (58.0.7):","     - ExpoModulesCore","+  - ExpoCrypto/Benchmarks (58.0.7):","+    - ExpoModulesCore","+    - ExpoModulesTestCore","+  - ExpoCrypto/Tests (58.0.7):","+    - ExpoModulesCore","+    - ExpoModulesTestCore","   - ExpoDevice (58.0.5):","     - ExpoModulesCore","   - ExpoDocumentPicker (58.0.4):","@@ -3404,6 +3410,8 @@ DEPENDENCIES:","   - ExpoContacts (from `../../../packages/expo-contacts/ios`)","   - ExpoContacts/Tests (from `../../../packages/expo-contacts/ios`)","   - ExpoCrypto (from `../../../packages/expo-crypto/ios`)","+  - ExpoCrypto/Benchmarks (from `../../../packages/expo-crypto/ios`)","+  - ExpoCry